## 2. Showroom car select (see the car while you pick it)

Replace any list or text-based car picker with a **3D showroom**, used for "Car Select" before a drive, the **Dealer**, and "My Cars".

- **Scene:** a dark, moody showroom with a polished reflective floor, soft spotlights and a slowly rotating turntable. The selected car sits on the turntable fully rendered: real model, current paint, installed parts, wheels.
- **Browsing:** left/right arrows (keyboard, gamepad bumpers, swipe on touch) slide to the next car with a quick camera pan. The next and previous cars are preloaded so swapping is instant.
- **Free look:** drag to orbit, scroll or pinch to zoom, and double-click to reset the view. The idle camera drifts slowly around the car.
- **Info panel** (like Forza's car cards, in our own style):
  - Name, year, archetype ("90s rotary coupe"), drivetrain badge (FR / AWD / MR).
  - **Class badge + rating** (e.g. **B 642**) with class colors: D, C, B, A, S1, S2, R. R is the top class, for race builds.
  - **Stat bars, 0–10:** Speed, Handling, Acceleration, Launch, Braking, Drift.
  - **Specs:** power (hp), torque, weight, front weight %, 0–100 km/h, top speed.
  - Price (Dealer), "OWNED" or "LOCKED – Level 8" state.
- **Actions:** Select / Buy / Test Drive. In Dealer, a paint-color picker previews the color live on the car before buying.
- **Filters:** owned, class, drivetrain, price.
- **Mobile:** works in portrait and landscape, with large touch targets.

**Done when:** you can scroll through every car, each shows as its real 3D model with correct paint and parts, and the stats and 0–100 match the simulation.

