## 5. Akagiri Touge: the Japanese mountain pass

A proper Japanese touge, the heart of drift culture. Add it as a **new location** and also connect it into the Open Road loop.

### 5.1 The road
- About **6–8 km** from the **base town** to the **summit**, ~**450 m** of elevation change. A narrow two-lane road (6–7 m wide) with a dashed center line.
- **Corners:** 35+ corners, including **10+ hairpins** (switchbacks stacked up the mountainside), fast flowing esses, a long downhill straight into a tight hairpin, a blind crest, a decreasing-radius corner, and one famous "**five consecutive hairpins**" section.
- **Roadside details:**
  - Steel guardrails (white posts, some dented), concrete **gutters (mizo)** on the inside of some corners that you can hook a wheel into.
  - Rock walls with **netting**, chevron arrow boards, **round curve mirrors** on blind corners, kilometer posts, speed signs in Japanese style.
  - Cliff drops with distant valley views, cedar and maple forest that follows the season.
- **Landmarks:** a **summit parking lot** (night meet spot with vending machines, a toilet block and a view over the city lights), a **red torii gate and small shrine** halfway up, a short **tunnel**, an **onsen (hot spring) town** at the base with lanterns and wooden buildings, and a closed rest stop.
- **Night:** sodium streetlights only on some sections, so most of the road is lit by your headlights. Glowing vending machines, and city lights in the valley.
- **Seasons:** sakura petals in spring, deep green and cicadas in summer, red/orange **momiji** in autumn (the signature look), and snow banks with icy patches in winter (lower grip).

### 5.2 Ways to play it
- **Downhill and Uphill time attack:** ghost, sector splits, medals.
- **Touge Battle (1 vs 1):** the classic Japanese cat-and-mouse format. Run 1: you lead and the rival chases; run 2: you swap. The chaser wins by closing the gap and the leader by pulling away. An AI rival has a personality and a signature car. Night by default.
- **Drift zones** on named sections (e.g. "Five Hairpins", "Shrine Bend", "Tunnel Exit"), scored with the skill chain.
- **Tandem Chase** from the original spec, following an AI lead car down the mountain.
- **Free drive** with light oncoming traffic (optional toggle) and the summit meet as a hangout spot.
- Available in Open Road (connected) and in Drift Track/event selection (as closed-road events).

**Done when:** a scripted downhill run completes without falling through the world, the elevation profile matches, every landmark is present, all four seasons render, and a touge battle can be won and lost.

