## 7. Final verification

1. `npm run build` passes, all vitest tests pass (physics, acceleration targets, part effects, rating/class, economy, save migration).
2. **Playwright end-to-end run:** title → car select (scroll 3 cars) → buy a part in the shop (check the install animation plays and the part is visible) → Open Road drive for 20 s → Akagiri Touge downhill for 30 s → touge battle start → multiplayer two-page test. Save screenshots to `screenshots/update-4/` and **look at every screenshot yourself**. Fix anything floating, clipping, mis-scaled, backwards, untextured, ugly or unreadable before finishing.
3. Hold 60 fps on the Medium preset in the garage (engine bay open) and on the touge at night with traffic.
4. No real brand names or logos anywhere (check models, part names, decals and UI).
5. Update `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `CREDITS.md`, `DECISIONS.md` and `MULTIPLAYER_SETUP.md`, then commit.
6. If you run out of room, stop at a clean step and write `NEXT_STEPS.md` saying exactly where to continue.

Start with Section 1 now.
